ID: B3-Ch06b-Rematch
TEXT:

Footsteps shake the paving stones. The chatter dies across our circle as the street goes dead quiet. Hadrik takes three heavy strides forward, widening the gap between us so we do not catch the backblast when two giant-blooded brawlers collide. The silence stretches, tight as a drawn bowstring.

Gontrok rounds the corner. Hadrik drops his stance, boots grinding into the dust, forearms locked across his chest. Gontrok does not slow. He barrels down the center of the avenue, locks onto Hadrik two dozen paces out, and surges forward in an explosive sprint, his right fist cocked like a siege engine.

Hadrik catches the blow on crossed vambraces. The shockwave sends his boots skimming backward through the gravel, but he stays upright, skidding to a halt with his jaw set. Gontrok lowers his fist, flashing a broad, venomous grin.

"I have been waiting for this," Gontrok says. "I hope you brought more than excuses, Hadrik."

"More than you can handle," Hadrik grunts.

"Good. Then let us see how much you-- wait." Gontrok stops mid-step, head snapping toward Kelrim. His finger jabs forward. "I know that goblin. Rebel courier. If you lot are traveling with him, then..."

The realization settles across his face, curling into a triumphant sneer.

"I knew it!" he barks, projecting across the street. "You spent the whole hunt hiding under our boots! Sheltered by that rat-king and his sewer rats. I told the king those tunnel dwellers were traitors waiting to turn, but our dear captain kept shielding his old pet student, swearing the underground was harmless. I cannot wait to hear how he defends them now!"

choice(""Actually, the king of the underground is not our friend. He even attacked us this morning!"", B3-Ch06b-Underground, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Underground)
choice(""They only offered us temporary shelter. There's no need to get them involved in this."", B3-Ch06b-Temporary, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Temporary)
choice(""Hey, if you want to attack the king of the underground, it's fine by me. I never liked the guy."", B3-Ch06b-Liked, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Liked)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Underground
TEXT:

"Actually, the king of the underground is not our friend. He even attacked us this morning!" I call out.

"So he came to his senses once he realized who he was harboring?" Gontrok sneers. "Does not change a thing. First the rebels, now you. That underground rat works against Ollendor, and I will see him hang for it."

"Hey, Gontrok," Hadrik cuts in. "Do you think you have time to chat in the middle of a challenge?"

"Be serious," Gontrok laughs. "I am playing with you. I know every move you have. Nothing you do can surprise me in the slight--"

Hadrik launches forward, covering the gap in a single bound. In the space of a heartbeat, his frame swells to standard human height, and a heavy leather boot slams into Gontrok's jaw. The impact sends the giant crashing into the nearest stone wall.

"Heh..." Gontrok pushes off the masonry, wiping a smear of blood from his split lip. His eyes narrow at Hadrik's human-sized frame. "You wore that dwarf skin so long I almost forgot your real proportions. Nice trick. What now? Stay human-sized and pray it throws off my timing?"

"No," Hadrik says. "Here is what comes next."

Hadrik charges again. He feints a high jab at the face, then snaps down into dwarf form mid-stride, burying a reinforced fist straight into Gontrok's gut. Gontrok leaps back to break distance. Hadrik pursues, instantly stretching back to human height. Gontrok anticipates the high punch and throws a cross to the bridge of Hadrik's nose, but his knuckles hit empty air—Hadrik shrinks back to a dwarf and cracks a low kick across Gontrok's shin.

For the next thirty seconds, Hadrik shifts sizes with every strike, alternating between dwarf, human, and leprechaun proportions to scramble Gontrok's reads. Gontrok reels under the relentless barrage. For the first time since we met him, the royal guard is purely on defense, unable to mount a single counter. Bruised and bleeding, Gontrok morphs the skin of his back into the quilled hide of an archer porcupine, spins on his heel, and launches a volley of barbed quills at Hadrik at twice the speed of any arena beast in Thilias.

Hadrik weaves through the first cluster, stone splintering where the quills embed, and hops backward to catch his breath.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Abysmal, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Abysmal)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Temporary
TEXT:

"They only offered us temporary shelter. There's no need to get them involved in this," I call out.

"Temporary or not, they knew who you were," Gontrok sneers. "The earl's death was broadcast last night. If that underground scum wanted loyalty, they would have chained you and handed you over at dawn. Walking around with one of their own proves where they stand."

"Hey, Gontrok," Hadrik cuts in. "Do you think you have time to chat in the middle of a challenge?"

"Be serious," Gontrok laughs. "I am playing with you. I know every move you have. Nothing you do can surprise me in the slight--"

