ID: B3-Ch06b-Liked
TEXT:

"Hey, if you want to attack the king of the underground, it's fine by me. I never liked the guy," I call out.

"Ungrateful words for the man who sheltered you," Gontrok sneers with visible disgust. "Have you no honor?"

"Guess not," I say, shrugging.

"Hey, Gontrok," Hadrik cuts in. "Do you think you have time to chat in the middle of a challenge?"

"Be serious," Gontrok laughs. "I am playing with you. I know every move you have. Nothing you do can surprise me in the slight--"

Hadrik launches forward, covering the gap in a single bound. In the space of a heartbeat, his frame swells to standard human height, and a heavy leather boot slams into Gontrok's jaw. The impact sends the giant crashing into the nearest stone wall.

