ID: B3-Ch06b-Warriors
TEXT:

"Yeah, get out of the way, Gontrok! Only real warriors are allowed here!"

"You think you are funny?" Gontrok's gaze snaps to me, murder in his eyes. "Let us see if you joke after I shatter your kneecaps."

"You will shatter nothing, Gontrok," the captain cuts in. "Your turn is done. We finish these criminals in seconds. Stand there and watch."

The words barely leave his lips before crushing pressure slams down on us. The sheer gravitational force drives my knees into the stone, pinning our limbs in an instant. Groaning under the weight, I strain to tilt my chin upward.

High above, the sky is choked with massive stone boulders suspended in midair, hovering like executioners' axes.

The earth elementalist drops the first volley, hurling several boulders straight at our pinned formation. Before the rocks crush us, Daren wrenches his sword arm upward and cuts a sharp horizontal line through the air. The captain's aura grip unravels instantly.

Kate reacts on instinct, throwing a canopy of reinforced ice over our heads. Hadrik launches into the air with a deafening war cry, pulverizing the heaviest falling boulder with a midair punch. Stone shrapnel gouges through Kate's ice canopy, but we scramble clear of the falling rubble.

"Hah!" Gontrok barks a harsh laugh. "What happened, Captain? Thought you had everything handled. Need a hand?"

"Quiet, fool," the captain barks. "They would be dead if you followed the plan."

"Shove your plan," Gontrok snarls. "I am nobody's lapdog—especially not yours."

"Illuna," I whisper, keeping my eyes forward. "If I keep them arguing, can you bring out those giant flying water serpents from yesterday?"

"I have been weaving the construct since they stepped into the street," Illuna murmurs. "I can release them, but these mages will shred them in open air. They need to be pinned first."

"I can drop a freeze wave across the perimeter," Kate whispers. "Huddle close so I do not catch you by mistake."

"Hadrik," I hiss under my breath. "Hadrik, hear me?... Damn it, he is not looking."

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Crumble, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Crumble)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Crumble
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 1) {
"Where is Loyrang?" Gontrok barks, glancing around. "He should be on the line."

"He had the same orders we did," says a blond elven royal guard with a wind mantle swirling around his wrists. "If he is absent, he is in open defiance of the king."

"He mentioned a herbalist shop," Gontrok grunts. "The district is crawling with them. He will be here."

"Stop making excuses for him," the elf snaps. "Your comrade deserted."

"Say that again," Gontrok growls, stepping into the elf's space.

"Hadrik!" Kate's whisper is sharp as broken glass.

Hadrik glances back. Kate jerks her chin toward our circle. Reading the gesture, Hadrik retreats with measured, backward steps, letting the guards bicker among themselves.

"What in the hell is happening out here?!" The Thilias ambassador's shrill voice cuts through the avenue. He stumbles out of the side alley behind the captain, purple robes bunched in his fists. "What are you idiots doing?"

"Ambassador, I ordered you into the safehouse until--" the captain barks.

"Silence, fool!" the ambassador shrieks, waving a manicured hand at us. "The earl's murderers are standing right in front of you! Why are they still breathing?! Stop arguing and kill them! Kill them now!"

Hadrik steps into our perimeter. Kate thrusts her palms outward, driving a radial wave of frost across the cobblestones. The elven wind mage snaps an air barrier into place, deflecting the cold. The captain hardens his aura into a translucent wall, shielding himself and the ambassador.

Two guards are too slow.

The frost wave slams into Gontrok and a hooded royal guard in a crimson cape, locking both in solid, frosted ice. Illuna does not hesitate. Three massive, serpentine constructs of water erupt from the street, churning through the air toward their marks. The lead serpent lunges for Gontrok and the frozen cape.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 0 && v_b3_ch6_secret != 0) {
"You hearing this, Loyrang?" Gontrok calls out. "They think they take this without us!"

"Do not speak to that deserter," says a blond elven royal guard with wind swirling at his wrists. "I caught him slipping toward the city gates. If I had not dragged him back, he would be halfway to the countryside."

"Watch your tongue," Gontrok growls, stepping into the elf's space. "That is my comrade. Take it back before I break your ribs."

"Save your breath, Gontrok," Loyrang mutters with a bored shrug. "He is thick as a stone post. Told him the whole walk I never received the king's summons, but he refused to listen."

"Hadrik!" Kate's whisper is sharp as broken glass.

Hadrik glances back. Kate jerks her chin toward our circle. Reading the gesture, Hadrik retreats with measured, backward steps, letting the guards bicker among themselves.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_secret == 0 && v_b3_ch6_tie == 0) {
"You hearing this, Loyrang?" Gontrok calls out. "They think they take this without us!"

"Do not speak to that deserter," says a blond elven royal guard with wind swirling at his wrists. "I caught him slipping toward the city gates. If I had not dragged him back, he would be halfway to the countryside."

"Watch your tongue," Gontrok growls, stepping into the elf's space. "That is my comrade. Take it back before I break your ribs."

"Save your breath, Gontrok," says Loyrang, the dark-skinned royal guard from our first encounter, leaning casually against a storefront. "He is thick as a stone post. Told him the whole walk I never received the king's summons, but he refused to listen."

"Hadrik!" Kate's whisper is sharp as broken glass.

Hadrik glances back. Kate jerks her chin toward our circle. Reading the gesture, Hadrik retreats with measured, backward steps, letting the guards bicker among themselves.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 0) {
"What in the hell is happening out here?!" The Thilias ambassador's shrill voice cuts through the avenue. He stumbles out of the side alley behind the captain, purple robes bunched in his fists. "What are you idiots doing?"

"Ambassador, I ordered you into the safehouse until--" the captain barks.

"Silence, fool!" the ambassador shrieks, waving a manicured hand at us. "The earl's murderers are standing right in front of you! Why are they still breathing?! Stop arguing and kill them! Kill them now!"

Hadrik steps into our perimeter. Kate thrusts her palms outward, driving a radial wave of frost across the cobblestones. The elven wind mage snaps an air barrier into place, shielding himself and Loyrang. The captain hardens his aura into a translucent wall, protecting himself and the ambassador.

Two guards are too slow.

The frost wave slams into Gontrok and a hooded royal guard in a crimson cape, locking both in solid, frosted ice. Illuna does not hesitate. Three massive, serpentine constructs of water erupt from the street, churning through the air toward their marks. The lead serpent lunges for Gontrok and the frozen cape.

}
Raw muscle fractures the ice around Gontrok. The giant bursts free of his frozen shell with a roar, diving sideways an instant before the water jaws snap shut. The crimson-caped guard has no such luck. The serpent swallows him whole, sweeping him skyward and carrying him far beyond the rooftops.

Across the street, the remaining two water serpents hit fierce resistance. The elven elementalist whips up a shrieking vortex of compressed air, grinding Illuna's construct to mist. The guard captain grips an empty space with both hands, his hardened aura shaping an invisible greatsword that shears clean through the third serpent's torso.

"Stay behind me, Ambassador," the captain commands, water splashing over his boots. "I have you."

"There," Illuna murmurs, eyes fixed on the alley. "The ambassador is their anchor. Threaten him, and their line breaks."

"Agreed," Kate says, frost gathering along her fingers. "Force the captain onto defense."

choice(""You guys take care of him. I'll go deal with the earth elementalist in the sky."", B3-Ch06b-Defend, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Defend, v_b3_ch6_focus = 0)
choice(""Okay. I'll take care of the air elementalist elf in the meantime."", B3-Ch06b-Defend, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Defend, v_b3_ch6_focus = 1)
choice(""Alright, I'll focus my attacks on him too, then."", B3-Ch06b-Defend, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Defend, v_b3_ch6_focus = 2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Defend
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_focus == 0) {
"You guys take care of him. I'll go deal with the earth elementalist in the sky."

"Do not get reckless up there," Kate says.

"I won't."

"Kate, seal his escape route," Illuna commands.

"On it." Kate sweeps her arm back, slamming a thick wall of reinforced ice across the mouth of the alley behind the ambassador.

Illuna snaps two water whips against the pavement. The pressurized streams writhe like living cobras, hissing across the stones toward the ambassador's boots. Simultaneously, a jagged spear of ice erupts from the ground beneath him.

Having cleaved the serpent, the captain throws up a hemispherical aura shield, locking himself and the ambassador inside and deflecting both the ice spire and the water cobras.

"Do not just stand there!" the captain bellows at his men as Flower begins raining fire arrows against his barrier. "Defend the ambassador! Kill these criminals!"

"Yes, protect me!" the ambassador shrieks, retreating against the ice wall. "Protect me at all costs!"

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_focus == 1) {
"Okay. I'll take care of the air elementalist elf in the meantime."

"Do not get reckless over there," Kate says.

"I won't."

"Kate, seal his escape route," Illuna commands.

"On it." Kate sweeps her arm back, slamming a thick wall of reinforced ice across the mouth of the alley behind the ambassador.

Illuna snaps two water whips against the pavement. The pressurized streams writhe like living cobras, hissing across the stones toward the ambassador's boots. Simultaneously, a jagged spear of ice erupts from the ground beneath him.

Having cleaved the serpent, the captain throws up a hemispherical aura shield, locking himself and the ambassador inside and deflecting both the ice spire and the water cobras.

"Do not just stand there!" the captain bellows at his men as Flower begins raining fire arrows against his barrier. "Defend the ambassador! Kill these criminals!"

"Yes, protect me!" the ambassador shrieks, retreating against the ice wall. "Protect me at all costs!"

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_focus == 2) {
"Alright, I'll focus my attacks on him too, then."

"Cut off his retreat first," Illuna tells Kate.

"On it." Kate sweeps her arm back, slamming a thick wall of reinforced ice across the mouth of the alley behind the ambassador.

Illuna snaps two water whips against the pavement. The pressurized streams writhe like living cobras, hissing across the stones toward the ambassador's boots. Simultaneously, a jagged spear of ice erupts from the ground beneath him.

Having cleaved the serpent, the captain throws up a hemispherical aura shield, locking himself and the ambassador inside and deflecting both the ice spire and the water cobras.

"Do not just stand there!" the captain bellows at his men as Flower unleashes a volley of fire arrows and I open fire with my crossbow. "Defend the ambassador! Kill these criminals!"

"Yes, protect me!" the ambassador shrieks, retreating against the ice wall. "Protect me at all costs!"

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1) {
Hadrik launches back at Gontrok before the giant can process the captain's order. Gontrok adjusts his footing, blocking with heavy forearms, but Hadrik's rapid size shifts keep him purely reactive.

"Melindra, give me the updraft--"

The wind catches my boots before I finish the sentence.

"Thanks!" I kick off, rising smoothly into the air.

"Hey, morons," Arraka's voice crackles from the amulet, low enough for our ears alone. "Remember that sneak with the suppressed aura you wanted me to track? He is in that abandoned brick house on the corner."

A radiant blue silhouette flares to life on the exterior wall of the building, crowned with glowing blue lettering: 'I'm hiding here.'

A second later, a dozen ice javelins lance from Kate's hands, punching through the stone facade like paper. A stifled shriek cuts short inside, followed by the heavy thud of a collapsing body.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0) {
Hadrik launches back at Gontrok before the giant can process the captain's order. Gontrok adjusts his footing, blocking with heavy forearms, but Hadrik's rapid size shifts keep him purely reactive.

"Melindra, give me the updraft--"

The wind catches my boots before I finish the sentence.

"Thanks!" I kick off, rising smoothly into the air.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_focus == 1 && v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1) {
"Dreymarr!" the captain roars, straining to hold his barrier against the barrage. "Report! Dreymarr!"

The house remains dead silent. The ice javelins left no room for survival.

"Daren, Leila, let us take the air elementalist together," I say, hovering ten feet up. "I draw his focus, you two close in for the finish."

'Understood,' Leila writes in glowing script.

"Should I take point?..." Daren asks, adjusting his shield grip.

"No need. I have this."

I bank hard through the air, heading straight for the elven air elementalist.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_focus == 1 && v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0) {
