'Understood,' Leila writes in glowing script.

"Should I take point?..." Daren asks, adjusting his shield grip.

"No need. I have this."

I bank hard through the air, heading straight for the elven air elementalist.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_focus == 0 && v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 || v_b3_ch6_focus == 2 && v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1) {
"Dreymarr!" the captain roars, straining to hold his barrier against the barrage. "Report! Dreymarr!"

The house remains dead silent. The ice javelins left no room for survival.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Earth, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Earth) if (v_b3_ch6_focus == 0)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Air, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Air) if (v_b3_ch6_focus == 1)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Ambassador, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Ambassador) if (v_b3_ch6_focus == 2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Air
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_perception < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_perception >= 3 && v_reflexes >= 3)
#if(v_perception < 3) {


As I close the distance, the air violently seizes my body, spinning me into a furious aerial vortex. I kick and thrash against the currents, but the rotational force locks my limbs tight.

"Finally, someone walks into my parlor," the elf sneers, his fingers drawing back. "I grew tired of waiting."

A razor-thin crescent of compressed air shrieks across the gap. The wind blade shears through my torso before my nervous system can register the hit, cutting me in two.

}
#if(v_perception >= 3 && v_reflexes < 3) {


As I close the distance, the wind across my face shifts with an unnatural, grinding friction. The flight currents beneath me shudder, catching on an unseen resistance in the air ahead.

I extend a hand. The air two feet out ripples with localized turbulence. Invisible vortex traps, woven across the entire approach.

"Leila, hold!" I shout, and she plants her boots on the cobblestones. "Daren, wind traps ahead! Sweep your blade as you advance to ground the weaves!"

My mouth barely closes before the elf hurls a whistling crescent of compressed air. It crosses the space faster than my eyes can track, severing my torso in a single heartbeat.

}
#if(v_perception >= 3 && v_reflexes >= 3) {


As I close the distance, the wind across my face shifts with an unnatural, grinding friction. The flight currents beneath me shudder, catching on an unseen resistance in the air ahead.

I extend a hand. The air two feet out ripples with localized turbulence. Invisible vortex traps, woven across the entire approach.

"Leila, hold!" I shout, and she plants her boots on the cobblestones. "Daren, wind traps ahead! Sweep your blade as you advance to ground the weaves!"

The elf whips his arm forward, releasing a whistling crescent of compressed wind. My reflexes take over—I torque my body midair, the blade grazing past my tunic and shearing stone from the wall behind me. Seeing the miss, the elf unleashes a rapid barrage of wind blades to overwhelm my evasion.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_perception < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_perception < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_perception < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Rating, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Rating) if (v_b3_ch6_selected == 3 && v_is_dead == 0 && v_perception >= 3 && v_reflexes >= 3)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Echoing, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Echoing) if (v_is_dead == 0 && v_perception >= 3 && v_reflexes >= 3 && v_b3_ch6_selected != 3)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Rating
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch6_assist,1)
set(v_b3_ch6_air,2)
achievement("Nice assist",v_ac_b3_ch6_assist)
As I weave through the barrage of air scythes, a metallic voice blares from right behind my ear.

"Warning! Warning!" announces the green-eyed drone still tailing my flight path. "Non-combat unit under attack. Requesting immediate tactical support."

"What is that?..." The elf falters, halting his casting to gawk at the sky.

A flight of red-eyed combat drones plummets through the clouds, converging on the elven mage with mechanical precision.

"Get away from me, metal vermin!" The elf hurls wind blades upward, but the drones bank cleanly around the projectiles.

"Now!" I yell down to Leila and Daren. "Close in while he is split!"

A six-headed hydra of compressed wind materializes between us and the elf, its translucent scales glinting in the morning sun. Daren and I pull up short, but Leila does not break stride. She charges straight through the howling construct without blinking.

Too absorbed in fighting off the drones to check his flank, the elf only notices her when a steel dagger punches through the back of his throat. Leila rips the blade free. Arterial blood fountains over the cobblestones. The elf clutches at his shredded neck with both hands, his knees folding beneath him. He hits the pavement face-first, drowning in his own blood.

"How did you know the hydra was hollow?" Daren asks as the air construct dissolves into a harmless breeze.

'I didn't,' Leila writes, wiping her dagger on her trousers. 'His focus was on the sky. No somatic triggers or focal gestures. An illusion to buy time.'

"Clean work," I say, dropping to the street. "And good timing, Overseer. Did not think having you follow me would pay off."

"Does this indicate satisfaction with your service interactions under the Overseer protocol?" the drone inquires.

"Sure. Five stars."

"Previous score of zero updated to five out of five," the drone states flatly. "Feedback logged. Question two waived. Have a pleasant day."

The green-eyed sphere turns upward, joining the combat drones as they ascend into the cloud cover.

At the edge of the alley, Loyrang leans against a doorframe, watching the corpses with mild detachment.

"Quick question," I say, nodding toward him. "Are you joining this fight or what?"

"Only if you force me," Loyrang replies.

"Fair enough."

A dark distortion tears through the air behind Kate. The black-robed assassin materializes mid-thrust, driving a dagger toward her spine.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Robed, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Robed)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Echoing
TEXT:

set(v_b3_ch6_air,0) if (v_b3_ch6_tie == 0 || v_b3_ch6_tie == 1 || v_ancient_languages < 2)
set(v_b3_ch6_air,1) if (v_ancient_languages >= 2)
#if(v_ancient_languages < 2) {


As I weave through the barrage of air scythes, an echoing voice rings out across the street from an untraceable origin.

The words are spoken in an unfamiliar elven dialect. The air elementalist barks a reply in the same tongue, then unleashes a sweeping gale that drives us back several yards.

The elf begins an elaborate rhythmic chant, weaving his hands in wide arcs. A six-headed hydra composed of howling wind solidifies in the center of the avenue, its translucent contours catching the glare of the morning sun.

"Hold back!" Daren calls out. "I will absorb the weave with my blade!"

Daren charges the monster, driving his enchanted broadsword straight into the hydra's chest. The blade passes through the wind construct with a hollow whoosh, drawing zero magical charge from the air.

"It is not catching!" Daren shouts, vaulting backward as two heads snap at his armor. "Fall back! Form up!"

We pull back out of striking distance. The hydra holds the center line, shielding the elf while he resumes firing wind scythes at our formation.

"Barry, Leila, behind my shield!" Daren yells from below. "Conserve your energy until we find an opening!"

We dive inside Daren's glowing aura barrier as wind scythes crash harmlessly against its perimeter.

}
#if(v_ancient_languages >= 2) {


As I weave through the barrage of air scythes, an echoing voice rings out across the street from an untraceable origin.

I catch the cadence immediately: an archaic Eastern elven dialect.

'Fake a somatic chant so I can anchor an illusionary wind hydra over your position,' the voice commands.

'Fine, but give me room to cast,' the elf replies in the same tongue, unleashing a sudden gale that shoves us back.

The elf begins an elaborate show of hand weaving. A six-headed hydra of howling wind solidifies before him, its translucent scales shimmering in the sun.

"Hold back!" Daren calls out, stepping forward. "I will absorb the weave with my blade!"

"Do not bother," I say. "I understood their speech. The hydra is pure illusion. Walk right through it."

"You are certain?" Daren asks, pausing.

"They used an obscure dialect so we would not catch the call. It is a bluff."

"Right behind you," Daren grunts, raising his shield and charging straight through the phantom monster alongside Leila.

I bank through the illusion on flight currents. We close in from three angles. The elf tries to channel another gale, but Leila slips behind his guard and drives her steel dagger deep into the back of his throat. Blood sprays across the stone as she pulls the blade free. The elf clutches his neck, choking on his own blood, and collapses to the pavement.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 0 && v_ancient_languages < 2) {
"What are you doing, traitor?" the elf snarls at Loyrang, who is leaning against the wall, watching with bored eyes. "Engage them!"

"Do not really feel like it," Loyrang mutters. "Maybe later."

"The king will hear of this!"

"Right," Loyrang says.

The elf's wind scythes continue battering Daren's shield, but the barrier holds firm. A dark distortion tears through the air behind Kate. The black-robed assassin materializes mid-thrust, driving a dagger toward her spine.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 1 && v_ancient_languages < 2) {
The elf's wind scythes continue battering Daren's shield, but the barrier holds firm. A dark distortion tears through the air behind Kate. The black-robed assassin materializes mid-thrust, driving a dagger toward her spine.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 0 && v_ancient_languages >= 2) {
I glance over at Loyrang, who has remained propped against the wall throughout the entire clash. The dark-skinned guard shows no sign of drawing steel.

"Quick question," I say. "Are you joining this fight or what?"

"Only if you force me," Loyrang replies.

"Fair enough."

A dark distortion tears through the air behind Kate. The black-robed assassin materializes mid-thrust, driving a dagger toward her spine.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 1 && v_ancient_languages >= 2) {
A dark distortion tears through the air behind Kate. The black-robed assassin materializes mid-thrust, driving a dagger toward her spine.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Robed, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Robed)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Earth
TEXT:

Updrafts carry me skyward into the floating quarry hovering above the avenue.

The boulder count has nearly doubled since the opening clash. The elementalist has spent every second of our street skirmish manufacturing heavy ordnance. With no active targets engaging him in the air, he has turned the sky above Ollendor into a stockpile.

I thread through the perimeter, banking between hovering granite masses in search of the caster.

Dozens of tons of reinforced stone hang suspended on delicate magical tethers. If I put a blade through the mage's throat, the suspension will snap, dropping the entire payload straight onto the street. Then again, leaving him alive gives him time to launch them at terminal velocity.

#if(v_b3_ch6_selected == 3) {
If I can force him to disperse the field, good. If not, a shout will give the circle below enough time to raise barriers before the avalanche hits.

The green-eyed drone bobs along in my wake, its propeller buzzing steadily against the wind. At this rate, a drifting slab will swat it out of the air and solve my survey problem permanently.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_selected != 3) {
If I can force him to disperse the field, good. If not, a shout will give the circle below enough time to raise barriers before the avalanche hits.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Earth2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Earth2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Earth2
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_bluff < 3 || v_magical_sense < 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b3_ch6_concealed == 0 && v_bluff >= 3 && v_magical_sense >= 2 || v_b3_ch6_concealed == 1 && v_bluff >= 3 && v_magical_sense >= 2)
#if(v_magical_sense < 2) {


Drifting aimlessly through the stone thicket yields nothing. I close my eyes and reach outward, searching for the telltale hum of an active aura.

Ten seconds pass in dead silence. Nothing registers. The elementalist's suppression is absolute; the sky feels entirely empty.

A deafening rush of displaced air roars behind me. Two multi-ton boulders converge from opposite flanks at blinding speed, crushing my skull before I can twist my torso to evade.

}
#if(v_magical_sense >= 2) {


Drifting aimlessly through the stone thicket yields nothing. I close my eyes and focus my magical sense, sifting through the ambient background noise.

A faint, tightly wrapped signature pulses nearby. I open my eyes and lock onto the source, but find only an enormous, irregularly shaped boulder. Not behind the rock. Inside it. The caster has hollowed out the core and rides within the stone.

The air thunders as two flanking boulders slam toward my head from left and right. I bank downward, letting the stones collide with a bone-jarring crash, and surge straight for the hollow boulder with steel drawn.

The elementalist reacts instantly. The boulder banks hard, carving an escape vector through the floating mass as half the orbiting rocks part to let him pass and the rest accelerate straight at me.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_selected == 3 && v_magical_sense >= 2) {
A tumbling boulder clips the drone trailing my flight path.

"Warning! Warning!" the green eye flashes frantically. "Non-combat unit under attack. Requesting immediate tactical--"

A second slab pulverizes the sphere into scrap metal, sending the mangled wreckage spiraling to the streets below. The remaining boulders wheel around, closing my escape angles.

Dodging takes every ounce of aerial coordination I possess. The elementalist keeps widening the gap, and dodging a dozen guided projectiles leaves zero room to mount an offense.

}
#if(v_magical_sense >= 2 && v_b3_ch6_selected != 3) {
The swarm wheels around, boxing my trajectory from all sides. Dodging takes every ounce of aerial coordination I possess. The elementalist keeps widening the gap, and evading a dozen guided projectiles leaves zero room to mount an offense.

}
#if(v_magical_sense >= 2 && v_bluff < 3) {
The net tightens. The boulders converge from six directions simultaneously, cutting off every flight line. The stones collide at the center, crushing me instantly.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_concealed == 0 && v_bluff >= 3 && v_magical_sense >= 2) {
He is tracking me through magical sense. The boulders only home in because my aura is radiating across the sky.

Mid-evasion, I draw my presence inward, collapsing my aura according to the discipline Illuna demonstrated.

The guidance snaps. The incoming boulders lose their trajectory, drifting to a dead halt in midair like tethered balloons.

He has lost my position, but his muffled core still glows on my mental map. I can drop back to support the circle below, or hunt the earth mage while he is blind.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_concealed == 1 && v_bluff >= 3 && v_magical_sense >= 2) {
He is tracking me through magical sense. The boulders only home in because my aura is radiating across the sky.

Mid-evasion, I draw my presence inward, locking down my aura just as I did before the street fight started.

The guidance snaps. The incoming boulders lose their trajectory, drifting to a dead halt in midair like tethered balloons.

He has lost my position, but his muffled core still glows on my mental map. I can drop back to support the circle below, or hunt the earth mage while he is blind.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_bluff < 3 || v_magical_sense < 2)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_bluff < 3 || v_magical_sense < 2)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_bluff < 3 || v_magical_sense < 2)
choice("Go back down.", B3-Ch06b-Visibility, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Visibility, v_b3_ch6_earth = 0) if (v_bluff >= 3 && v_magical_sense >= 2)
choice("Keep going after the earth elementalist.", B3-Ch06b-Mustache, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Mustache, v_b3_ch6_earth = 1) if (v_bluff >= 3 && v_magical_sense >= 2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Visibility
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 1) {
Hunting the elementalist through this maze will take time we do not have. I need to see what is happening on the ground.

I dive clear of the boulder field and scan the street below. Hadrik is locked in close-quarters trading with Gontrok, holding his own. Daren and Leila are pinned behind a defensive aura shield, holding off the air elementalist's wind hydra.

Kate and Flower continue hammering the captain and ambassador with ranged spells, but a black-robed royal guard is teleporting across their flanks, hurling conjured steel at Kate and Illuna. They are split between suppressing the captain and parrying the assassin.

I angle my descent to drop behind the teleporting rogue.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 0) {
Hunting the elementalist through this maze will take time we do not have. I need to see what is happening on the ground.

I dive clear of the boulder field and scan the street below. Hadrik is locked in close-quarters trading with Gontrok, holding his own. Daren and Leila are pinned behind a defensive aura shield against the air elementalist's wind hydra, while Loyrang watches from the sideline.

Kate and Flower continue hammering the captain and ambassador with ranged spells, but a black-robed royal guard is teleporting across their flanks, hurling conjured steel at Kate and Illuna. They are split between suppressing the captain and parrying the assassin.

I angle my descent to drop behind the teleporting rogue.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Robed, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Robed)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Mustache
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch6_peek,1) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength >= 4 || v_strength >= 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength < 4 || v_strength < 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength >= 4 || v_strength >= 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
achievement("Peek-a-boo!",v_ac_b3_ch6_peek)


A clean opening like this will not come twice. The team can hold the line a little longer while I take the artillery off the board.

Tracking his muffled signature, I drift from boulder to boulder with my aura locked down tight. I glide within arm's reach of the hollow rock without alerting him. The shell needs ventilation and cockpit space, which means the granite walls cannot be more than a few inches thick.

Even so, the stone is magically reinforced. Breaching it in a single strike demands serious leverage.

#if(v_strength < 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
I draw my scimitar for the reach, squaring my shoulders against the floating boulder, and put all my weight into a two-handed cleave.

The reinforced granite resists the edge. The blade bites halfway and binds. Before I can wrench it free, the surrounding boulders awaken, converging from every angle to crush me in the air.

}
#if(v_strength >= 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
I draw my scimitar for the reach, squaring my shoulders against the floating boulder, and put all my weight into a two-handed cleave.

Augmented strength drives the curved blade clean through the reinforced stone. The top half of the boulder shears off and drifts away. Curled in the hollow bottom sits a man in his fifties sporting a bushy mustache, ducking from the strike.

I drop behind him before he finds his footing and press cold steel against his jugular.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength < 4) {
My fifteen-inch dagger lacks the sweep of a larger blade, but Daren's enchantments give it razor sharpness. I brace my footing in midair and drive the point into the stone.

The reinforced granite resists the shallow thrust. The dagger binds in the rock face. Before I can strike again, the surrounding boulders awaken, converging from every angle to crush me in the air.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength >= 4) {
My fifteen-inch dagger lacks the sweep of a larger blade, but Daren's enchantments give it razor sharpness. I brace my footing in midair and drive the point into the stone.

Augmented strength forces the enchanted blade through the shell in a clean, brutal shearing motion. The stone lid splits and drifts free. Curled inside sits a man in his fifties with a bushy mustache, cowering from the blow.

I slip behind him as he scrambles upward, resting the dagger's edge against his throat.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength < 4 || v_strength < 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength < 4 || v_strength < 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength < 4 || v_strength < 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
choice("Kill him.", B3-Ch06b-Retaliate, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Retaliate) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength >= 4 || v_strength >= 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
choice("Try to convince him to make the boulders disappear.", B3-Ch06b-Convince, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Convince) if (v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength >= 4 || v_strength >= 3 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Convince
TEXT:

"Listen," I say. "Whatever the king pays you, we can negotiate a better deal if you--"

A needle-sharp stone spire erupts from the rock beneath my boots, impaling my right hand. The weapon clatters from numb fingers. The elementalist rolls off the platform onto a freshly conjured stone ledge below, snapping his fingers as hundreds of suspended boulders converge on my position. Trapped with no flight vector, I am crushed beneath tons of falling granite.

choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Ambassador
TEXT:

"I am flanking the captain," I say, rising into the air currents. "An attack from above forces him to split his focus."

"Watch the sky," Illuna warns. "The earth elementalist can release those boulders at any second."

"Understood. Be right back."

I bank wide around the intersection, climbing twenty paces above the captain's perimeter. I loosed three crossbow bolts in rapid succession; each quarrel ricochets off his translucent aura dome with a dull crack. While cranking the lever to reload, I project my voice over the street.

"Hey, Ambassador! Long time no see!"

"Do not speak to me, murderer!" the ambassador screeches back, clutching his embroidered robes. "I will see you flayed alive!"

"We already paid our toll in Thilias," I say, putting two more bolts against the captain's shield. "You designed an entire arena bloodsport to execute us, and we walked out. Not my fault your death traps are as incompetent as your diplomacy."

"Silence!" The ambassador's face turns purple with rage. "This is not Thilias! No gnome king or arena master will save you here! The royal guard and the entire garrison of Ollendor answer to my command for one purpose—your execution!"

"I know, and I appreciate it," I shout back. "Imagine the trouble we would be in if the garrison were commanded by someone competent."

"Enough!" the ambassador roars, grabbing the captain's shoulder. "Captain, execute him! Now!"

"Ambassador, striking upward thins the barrier," the captain grunts, straining under Flower's fire volley. "Your safety will be compro--"

"I do not care!" the ambassador screams. "Kill him! That is an order!"

choice("Try to shoot the ambassador while the barrier is weakened.", B3-Ch06b-Weakened, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Weakened)
choice("Fly back to Kate and Illuna.", B3-Ch06b-Fly, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Fly)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Weakened
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_selected == 3) {
"As you command, Ambassador..." the captain growls.

He thrusts his right arm upward, closes his fist, and yanks downward as if gripping an invisible hawser. Gravitational force seizes my limbs, dragging me ten feet toward the street before I tear free of the vector and snap my crossbow onto the ambassador.

"Warning! Warning!" blares the green-eyed drone circling my flank. "Aura manipulation detected within proximity coordinates. Cease immediately or tactical support will engage."

"Overseer unit, stand down," the captain barks. "Clear the airspace."

"Error. Command rejected."

With the captain's focus fractured, the dome above the ambassador flickers. I loose two bolts through the seam. One punches deep into the right side of the ambassador's chest.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_selected != 3) {
"As you command, Ambassador..." the captain growls.

He thrusts his right arm upward, closes his fist, and yanks downward as if gripping an invisible hawser. Gravitational force seizes my limbs, dragging me ten feet toward the street before I tear free of the vector and snap my crossbow onto the ambassador.

With the captain's focus diverted, the dome above the ambassador flickers. I loose two bolts through the seam. One punches deep into the right side of the ambassador's chest.

}
"Got him!" I call out.

The words die in my throat. Crushing downward pressure slams into my back, pinning me hard against the exterior curvature of the captain's barrier. My ribs groan under the weight; my limbs lock rigid.

Through the translucent dome beneath me, the captain draws an enchanted stiletto. He thrusts upward. The magically honed steel punches through the barrier seam and drives into the base of my skull, severing my brainstem in a fraction of a second.

choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Fly
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_selected == 3) {
"As you command, Ambassador..." the captain growls.

He thrusts his right arm upward, closes his fist, and yanks downward as if gripping an invisible hawser. Crushing pressure seizes my frame, dragging me ten feet down, but I twist into the flight currents and accelerate away with everything Melindra's wind can give me. The tether frays with distance—holding the defensive dome limits his offensive reach.

"Warning! Warning!" the green-eyed drone buzzes behind me. "Aura manipulation detected within proximity coordinates. Cease immediately or tactical support will engage."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_selected != 3) {
"As you command, Ambassador..." the captain growls.

He thrusts his right arm upward, closes his fist, and yanks downward as if gripping an invisible hawser. Crushing pressure seizes my frame, dragging me ten feet down, but I twist into the flight currents and accelerate away with everything Melindra's wind can give me. The tether frays with distance—holding the defensive dome limits his offensive reach.

}
"What are you doing, fool?!" the ambassador shrieks from below. "He is escaping!"

"The farther he flies, the less threat he poses to your position," the captain snaps. "He dies in due time. Maintain discipline."

The ambassador trembles with rage but clamps his jaw shut. One final surge of wind tears me clear of the captain's tether, carrying me back toward Kate and Illuna's position.

Across the intersection, a black-robed royal guard is blinking through short-range teleports, hurling conjured daggers at Kate and Illuna. Kate and Flower are locked into suppressing the captain, leaving Illuna to swat at the teleporter with water whips.

Daren remains occupied holding his aura shield over Leila against the air elementalist.

I bank my descent to take the black-robed assassin from the blind spot behind his shoulder.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Robed, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Robed)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Robed
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch6_credo,1) if (v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0 && v_b3_ch5_fight >= 4)
