ID: B3-Ch06b-Dome
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_defense == 1) {
"I say it's still worth it. We're going to need every possible defense against that many rocks."

"Understood," Kate says. "I will hold a light shell and pour in reinforcement when the heavy mass hits."

"Daren, Leila!" I shout across the street. "Form on us! Ice dome going up!"

Daren angles his shield against incoming wind scythes, covering Leila as they sprint across the cobblestones. Once inside Melindra's wind perimeter, Kate throws a vaulted dome of reinforced ice over our heads, and Daren layers his glowing aura shield across the outer crown.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_defense == 1 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
"I say it's still worth it. We're going to need every possible defense against that many rocks."

"Understood," Kate says. "I will hold a light shell and pour in reinforcement when the heavy mass hits."

"Daren, Leila!" I shout across the street. "Form on us! Ice dome going up!"

Daren and Leila sprint into our formation. Kate manifests a vaulted dome of reinforced ice over the group, and Daren locks his glowing aura barrier across the outer crown.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_defense == 0) {
"Alright. Let's keep the ice dome as a last alternative, then."

"Daren, Leila!" I shout across the street. "Incoming bombardment! Form on us!"

Daren angles his shield against incoming wind scythes, covering Leila as they sprint across the cobblestones. Once inside Melindra's wind perimeter, Daren reinforces our canopy with his glowing aura barrier.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_defense == 0 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
"Alright. Let's keep the ice dome as a last alternative, then."

"Daren, Leila!" I shout across the street. "Incoming bombardment! Form on us!"

Daren and Leila sprint into our formation. Daren plants his boots and projects his glowing aura barrier over Melindra's wind shield.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_defense == 1 || v_b3_ch6_defense == 1 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
"Will your shield hold against physical granite?" I ask Daren.

"The construct stops magical forces," Daren says, bracing both arms against the hilt. "Natural, non-magical stones will pass through the weave."

"Three stacked layers," I say, looking up at the shimmering barriers. "Better than open cobblestones."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_defense == 0 || v_b3_ch6_defense == 0 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
"Will your shield hold against physical granite?" I ask Daren.

"The construct stops magical forces," Daren says, bracing both arms against the hilt. "Natural, non-magical stones will pass through the weave."

"Melindra's wind will buffer the bleedthrough," I say. "Hold the line."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 || v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
The bombardment begins. The earth elementalist drops an opening salvo of ten boulders, testing the resilience of our defenses. Each multi-ton projectile shatters against Daren's aura shield in a cascade of dust and gravel.

Having measured our resistance, he releases the main payload. Fifty massive boulders scream down at terminal velocity, some blunt and heavy, others magically tapered into armor-piercing spikes. They hammer Daren's barrier in a relentless barrage; the energy barrier bends under the kinetic force, but deflects the mass across the perimeter.

Daren grunts through gritted teeth, holding the field stable. For a moment, the defense holds--

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Underneath, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Underneath) if (v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_defense == 1 || v_b3_ch6_defense == 1 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Blunder, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Blunder) if (v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_defense == 0 || v_b3_ch6_defense == 0 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Blunder
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_toughness < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_toughness >= 4)
#if(v_toughness < 4) {


Two natural granite stones bypass both magical barriers without losing momentum. One catches me square on the temple before I can shift my weight.

Bone splinters under the impact, and the world fades to black.

}
#if(v_toughness >= 4) {


Two natural granite stones bypass both magical barriers without losing momentum. One clips me hard across the temple.

Blunt trauma flares behind my eyes. Blood trickles through my hair, but reinforced bone integrity prevents a fracture. I shake off the ringing in my ears, locking my focus back on the fight. Drifting into analytical detachment on an active front line is a fast way to get buried.

"Barry, still with us?!" Kate calls out, throwing a translucent ice canopy over our circle.

"Still breathing," I grunt, pressing a hand to the swelling knot on my skull. "Toughness stat earned its keep."

"I will try to keep the captain suppressed while holding the dome," Kate says, "but dividing focus gives him room to counter."

"Drop the offense, Kate," Daren says, gesturing toward the sky where a fresh wave of a hundred boulders gathers momentum. "My shield is buckling, and wind barriers fold against physical stone. If unworked rocks come through, your ice is our only hard stop."

"Understood," Kate says, setting her jaw. "Pouring everything into structural reinforcement."

She channels her core reserves into the ice, turning the crystalline canopy thick and opaque. Exterior visibility vanishes, replaced by the deafening thunder of multi-ton boulders slamming into the roof.

The barrage is relentless. The elementalist hammers every quadrant, focusing ten consecutive strikes on a single seam to crack the weave. Kate reinforces the fracture points on the fly, matching each impact with fresh frost. The bombardment gradually tapers off as the sky empties of ammunition.

Before we can exhale, the ice canopy above us shatters under an overwhelming pulse of kinetic force. Gravitational pressure slams us face-down onto the cobblestones.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_toughness < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_toughness < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_toughness < 4)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Conditions, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Conditions) if (v_toughness >= 4)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Underneath
TEXT:

Two unworked boulders slip through Daren's energy barrier without slowing, but Kate's underlying ice canopy absorbs the impact with a sharp crack.

"Natural stone?" Kate asks Daren, eyes on the fractures.

"Unworked granite," Daren confirms. "Bypasses the energy weave entirely."

"I will reinforce the shell," Kate says. "Holding both the dome and offensive ice spikes against the captain will stretch my reserves, though."

"Drop the offense, Kate," Daren says, pointing up at the gathering wave of a hundred boulders. "My barrier is near its breaking point, and wind cannot stop dead weight. Your dome is the last line."

"Understood," Kate says. "Pouring everything into defense."

She channels her mana into the ice, turning the translucent vault thick and milky white. Outside visibility cuts out just as Daren's barrier shatters, leaving our canopy to take the direct brunt of the bombardment.

The stones hammer the dome like siege artillery. The elementalist tests the perimeter, focusing ten consecutive strikes onto a single structural rib. Kate counters each impact with fresh frost, reinforcing the stress points until the roar above finally dies down. The ammunition has run dry.

Before we can catch our breath, the ice canopy disintegrates under a crushing wave of kinetic force. Gravitational pressure drives us flat against the cobblestones.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Conditions, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Conditions)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Retaliate
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0 && v_b3_ch5_fight < 4) {
I draw the edge across his throat in a single fluid stroke. Blood geysers across the granite cockpit. I kick clear of the hollow boulder, diving toward the street on flight currents while the gravity tethers dissolve.

"Incoming boulders!" I bellow over the rush of wind. "Take cover!"

Kate reacts to my shout instantly, snapping an ice javelin through the head of the black-robed assassin as he turns toward my voice.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 || v_b3_ch5_fight >= 4) {
I draw the edge across his throat in a single fluid stroke. Blood geysers across the granite cockpit. I kick clear of the hollow boulder, diving toward the street on flight currents while the gravity tethers dissolve.

"Incoming boulders!" I bellow over the rush of wind. "Take cover!"

}
The sky collapses into chaos. The remaining royal guards scramble for shelter as hundreds of unsupported boulders rain across the street.

My companions cluster tight as Kate erects an emergency ice dome. Hovering directly above the canopy, I slash through the heaviest falling fragments with my blade, deflecting kinetic mass away from the apex.

The roar subsides as the last stones pulverize the pavement. Hadrik and Gontrok emerge from the dust cloud, trading heavy blows as if nothing fell. As Kate dismisses the cracked ice dome, a massive downward wave of kinetic force flattens us against the cobblestones, pinning our limbs rigid.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Conditions, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Conditions)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Conditions
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 || v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
Daren shifts his sword a fraction of an inch to the right, severing the unseen aura weave. He scrambles to his feet and charges the captain as the conjured stone debris around us dissolves into mist.

The captain thrusts both palms forward, hurling Daren back with an invisible kinetic wave while locking the rest of us back against the cobblestones. He wrenches his fingers to strip Daren's blade, but Daren's arm jerks forward with the weapon—the hilt remains bonded to his palm through hardened aura.

"Aura-binding the hilt to your flesh?" The captain's eyes narrow. "You picked up a parlor trick. However--"

A sickening crunch echoes down the street. Daren's wrist twists at an unnatural, agonizing angle. He stifles a roar of pain as his aura connection breaks; the broadsword tears free and snaps into the captain's waiting hand.

"--you remain an amateur," the captain says, tossing the blade into the gutter with contempt. "A simple torque breaks your focus. Lie in the dirt where your kind belongs."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0) {
Crushing downward force slams Daren back onto the stone beside us. His broadsword twitches in the dirt as he tries a remote recall, but wrist agony fractures his concentration.

The captain turns toward the alley brawl.

"Gontrok!" the captain barks. "Break this ice wall! The ambassador is trapped!"

Gontrok catches Hadrik's charging fist on an armored forearm, ducks under a sweeping hook, and grunts through gritted teeth. "Busy here, Captain!"

"Damn it." The captain's gaze snaps to the elven air elementalist. "Felsig! Get over here and cut a hole with wind magic! Do not execute the criminals on your way. That is an order!"

Felsig hesitates, air curling around his fingers. "Why leave them breathing?"

"Because they turn every spell cast at them back on the caster," the captain snaps. "You throw wind blades near them, they use them to cut their bonds or kill you. Ambassador's safety comes first. Move!"

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
Crushing downward force slams Daren back onto the stone beside us. His broadsword twitches in the dirt as he tries a remote recall, but wrist agony fractures his concentration.

The captain turns toward the alley brawl.

"Gontrok!" the captain barks. "Break this ice wall! The ambassador is trapped!"

Gontrok catches Hadrik's charging fist on an armored forearm, ducks under a sweeping hook, and grunts through gritted teeth. "Busy here, Captain!"

"Damn it." The captain glares skyward, barking over the street noise. "Bolwick! Report!"

Dead silence answers from the clouds.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_tie == 0) {
"What about Loyrang?" Felsig demands. "Send him to execute the criminals while I breach the ice. That traitor has not lifted a finger. Make him prove his loyalty!"

"If it gets you moving, fine!" the captain snaps. "Loyrang, execute them."

"Right, right," Loyrang mutters, ambling forward at a crawl. "On it, boss."

"Felsig, move!" the captain roars.

Felsig sprints toward the ice wall, leaving Loyrang trailing behind.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 && v_b3_ch6_tie == 1) {
"Moving now," Felsig says, sprinting toward the ice barricade.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 0 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
"Unresponsive..." the captain mutters. "Loyrang's blades cannot breach reinforced ice... Ambassador, circle through the main avenue and take the south alley back to the safehouse. Move!"

"Walk past the murderers with no escort?!" the ambassador shrieks. "What if they attack me?!"

"They are pinned to the cobblestones," the captain snaps. "I will project a mobile barrier over your advance. Go. I cannot hold this pressure indefinitely."

"If I take a scratch, your head rolls!" the ambassador cries, scurrying into the street.

"Understood. Move."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_tie == 1 && v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
"Unresponsive..." the captain mutters. "Ambassador, circle through the main avenue and take the south alley back to the safehouse. Move!"

"Walk past the murderers with no escort?!" the ambassador shrieks. "What if they attack me?!"

"They are pinned to the cobblestones," the captain snaps. "I will project a mobile barrier over your advance. Go. I cannot hold this pressure indefinitely."

"If I take a scratch, your head rolls!" the ambassador cries, scurrying into the street.

"Understood. Move."

}
choice("Ask Arraka if she can help Kate cancel the captain's aura technique like yesterday.", B3-Ch06b-Surrounded, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Surrounded, v_b3_ch6_uninjured = 0)
choice("Ask Daren if he can try summoning the sword with his uninjured hand instead.", B3-Ch06b-Surrounded, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Surrounded, v_b3_ch6_uninjured = 1)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Surrounded
TEXT:

