ID: B3-Ch06b-Trance
TEXT:

Rose's voice blares through the transceiver. The world freezes into absolute stillness—dust motes lock in place, and down the street, Hadrik and Gontrok hang suspended mid-strike.

"Barry, can you move?!" Rose calls out, her words tumbling in breathless haste.

"Rose?..." I strain against the stillness. "How did you know when to--"

"No time!" Rose cuts in. "The pressure above you—can you break free?"

"Still pinned," I grunt, testing my limbs against the stone. "The downward crush stopped, but the gravity field holds."

"No, no, no..." Panic bleeds into Rose's voice. "I thought this would break it! I cannot hold the freeze much longer... Please, find a way before the weave--"

"Are you seeing this?..." Daren's voice carries a strange, distant clarity. He stares into the frozen air above us.

"Seeing what, Daren? If you have a counter, play it now!"

"The flow lines," Daren breathes, eyes tracing unseen geometries in the air. "Locked in place like this, the weave is unmistakable. Arraka was right—threads tied into a knot."

"Daren, I can't... ugh..." Rose's voice fractures on the line. "Do whatever you see... I am losing consciousness..."

"Release the weave, Rose," Daren says in a steady, measured tone. "I have him."

"Right..."

Time snaps back into motion. Gravitational load crashes down with renewed fury, but Daren thrusts his left hand upward, snaps his fingers closed, and unweaves the captain's technique. The pressure vanishes instantly.

#if(v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 0) {
"Stand down, Captain," Daren says, rising from the cobblestones with steady, measured strides. "Yield now, and you live."

"Arrogant healer," the captain snarls. "Let us see your confidence after I break the other wrist."

The captain reaches out to torque Daren's left hand, but Daren executes a quick counter-flick, unraveling the force before it binds. The captain thrusts both palms forward in a kinetic wave; Daren meets it with a braced forearm, absorbing the shock without yielding an inch.

Daren extends his left hand. The broadsword leaps from the gutter, slapping cleanly into his open grip.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 1) {
"Stand down, Captain," Daren says, rising from the cobblestones with steady, measured strides. "Yield now, and you live."

"Arrogant healer," the captain snarls. "Let us see your confidence after I break the other wrist."

The captain reaches out to torque Daren's left hand, but Daren executes a quick counter-flick, unraveling the force before it binds. The captain thrusts both palms forward in a kinetic wave; Daren meets it with a braced forearm, absorbing the shock without yielding an inch.

Daren extends his left hand. The broadsword rips free of the captain's belt, slapping cleanly into Daren's open grip.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Trance2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Trance2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Trance2
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch6_freeze,1)
achievement("Time freeze enthusiast",v_ac_b3_ch6_freeze)
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0) {
"Stay back!" Felsig shouts, stepping beside the captain with air swirling around his fingers. "I'm warning you!"

The elf hurls a wind scythe. Daren catches the projectile on his broadsword, grounds the weave, and reflects the blade straight back. Felsig snaps a wind wall into place, then channels a tight vortex between them to block Daren's approach.

Daren steps directly into the gale, planting the tip of his broadsword into the eye of the vortex. The roaring whirlwind rapidly condenses, its rotational energy draining into the enchanted steel until it spins as a compact gray eddy around the fuller.

"What?!" Felsig shrieks. "Impossible!"

"Spin it all you want, wind is still an element," Daren says. "Take it back."

Daren sweeps the blade forward, releasing the miniature storm. The vortex expands to full scale as it barrels down the avenue, driving Felsig into a panicked retreat.

The captain sidesteps the whirlwind, but the opening is all Daren needs. Closing the distance in two strides, Daren drives his broadsword through the captain's chest.

The captain collapses into a widening pool of blood. Daren calmly sheathes his weapon and turns back to us.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
The captain unleashes consecutive kinetic waves, but with his sword in hand, Daren shears through each distortion with effortless precision.

Closing within striking range, the captain attempts a final desperate gambit, shaping his remaining aura into an invisible greatsword and swinging for Daren's neck.

Depleted of reserves, the translucent blade lacks density. Daren's enchanted steel cuts through the construct like glass and shears through the captain's neck in a single continuous arc.

The headless body thuds onto the cobblestones, blood pooling beneath the breastplate. Daren sheathes his blade and turns back to us.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Tactical, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Tactical)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Nausea
TEXT:

A flash of precognition seizes my mind: the captain clutches his temples in blinding agony, losing his grip on the aura field, followed instantly by a vision of Daren carrying Kelrim's limp corpse through the dust, grief etched into every line of his face.

Kelrim is readying the lethal feedback spell. He plans to burn his own nervous system to shatter the captain's hold.

The crushing pressure on my ribs makes every breath agony, but the choice is right in front of me.

choice("Tell Kelrim to not cast the nausea spell.", B3-Ch06b-Touching, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Touching, v_b3_ch6_kelrim = 1)
choice("Don't say anything to Kelrim.", B3-Ch06b-Panic, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Panic, v_b3_ch6_kelrim = 2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Touching
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch6_guardian,1) if (v_b3_ch6_manipulators == 2)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b3_ch6_manipulators != 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b3_ch6_manipulators == 2 && v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 0 || v_b3_ch6_manipulators == 2 && v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 1)
achievement("Guardian angel",v_ac_b3_ch6_guardian)
"Kelrim, don't do it!" I yell over the groan of crushed stone. "Don't cast the nausea spell!"

"What?..." Kelrim turns his head, straining against the cobblestones. "How did you know--"

"Do not throw your life away," I tell him. "We find a way out of this together!"

"We die otherwise!" Kelrim shouts back. "Better just me. I am only a goblin—goblins die every day. Nobody will grieve for me!"

"Kelrim!" Daren's roar cuts through the pain. "Do not speak like that! I forbid it! We walk out together or we fall together. Nobody gets left behind!"

"Touching sentiment," the captain sneers from above. "Your wish is granted. You die together."

#if(v_b3_ch6_manipulators != 2) {
The gravitational load intensifies, crushing consciousness from my mind. Kate and Flower fire weak, desperate projectiles, but the captain deflects them with casual wrist movements. Daren strains to summon his blade, his aura connection too fragmented to bridge the gap.

As darkness encroaches, Arraka's words from dawn echo in my memory: 'You have a natural affinity for aura manipulation.'

Did anyone else in the circle carry that potential? Could training have changed this outcome?... Pointless speculation. My lungs give out under the weight, and the darkness takes us all.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_manipulators == 2) {
The crushing pressure suddenly vanishes. We scramble off the pavement, gasping for air, while the captain stares at Kate with open disbelief.

"You broke the weave?!" the captain barks, pointing at the frost crystals lingering on her fingers. "With an icicle?! What kind of crude improvisation is this?!"

Kate holds an enchanted shard of ice, having copied Daren's untangling technique with pure tactile precision.

She answers with a volley of frost spikes, joined by Flower's fire arrows and Illuna's water lances. Kate and Illuna are nearing exhaustion, but Flower continues channeling full-power fire constructs.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_manipulators == 2 && v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 0) {
Under covering fire from our casters and my crossbow, Daren charges the captain. He extends his left hand; his broadsword tears free of the gutter and snaps into his grip. The captain raises both hands, repelling Daren with continuous kinetic shockwaves to keep him outside striking range.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_manipulators == 2 && v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 1) {
Under covering fire from our casters and my crossbow, Daren charges the captain. He extends his left hand; his broadsword rips free of the captain's belt and snaps into his grip. The captain raises both hands, repelling Daren with continuous kinetic shockwaves to keep him outside striking range.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b3_ch6_manipulators != 2)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_b3_ch6_manipulators != 2)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_b3_ch6_manipulators != 2)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Wyvern, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Wyvern) if (v_b3_ch6_manipulators == 2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Wyvern
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 || v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
"Hey, Daren, your armor has fire protection on it, right?" Flower calls out.

"It does," Daren calls back. "Why--"

"Perfect!"

A massive wyvern woven from roaring flames swoops down from the sky, snatching Daren in its blazing talons. It banks sharply, rocketing toward the captain.

"Flames are solidified with reinforcement magic!" Flower shouts after him. "No chance of dropping you! Probably!"

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
The captain attempts to repel the airborne assault with kinetic pulses, but the aura waves cannot halt the combined momentum of the armored warrior and the fire construct.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0) {
The captain attempts to repel the airborne assault with kinetic pulses, but the aura waves cannot halt the combined momentum of the armored warrior and the fire construct.

Felsig fires three wind scythes in rapid succession. Daren takes two on his shield, absorbs the third with his broadsword, and reflects it back at the elf. Felsig raises a frantic wind wall, panics, and casts an uncontrolled updraft around himself, flailing into the sky like a leaf caught in a gale.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_air == 0 || v_b3_ch6_air >= 1) {
As the wyvern dives for the kill, the captain settles into a two-handed swordsman's stance. Hardened aura outlines an invisible greatsword as he swings with all his remaining strength, cleaving the flame wyvern in two.

Daren drops from the dissolving construct, landing squarely inside the captain's guard.

The captain attempts a desperate follow-up slash with his translucent blade, but his depleted reserves cannot maintain its density. Daren's enchanted broadsword shears through the construct and cleaves the captain's neck in a single fluid stroke.

The headless body collapses into a pool of blood. Daren sheathes his sword and turns back to the group.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Tactical, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Tactical)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Panic
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim != 2) {
The crushing pressure suddenly breaks as the captain clutches his temples with a muffled groan of agony. He attempts to re-establish the gravity field, but the migraine shatters his focus, forcing him behind a personal barrier instead.

"A headache?..." Daren scrambles up, panic in his eyes. "Kelrim, tell me you did not cast that spell... Kelrim?..."

Illuna kneels beside the goblin, two fingers pressed to his carotid artery. She looks up, her expression grim. "He is gone."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim == 2) {
I keep my silence. If Kelrim has made his peace with the cost, shouting will only alert the captain and waste the sacrifice.

The crushing pressure breaks as the captain clutches his temples with a muffled groan of agony. He attempts to re-establish the gravity field, but the migraine shatters his focus, forcing him behind a personal barrier instead.

"A headache?..." Daren scrambles up, panic in his eyes. "Kelrim, tell me you did not cast that spell... Kelrim?..."

Illuna kneels beside the goblin, two fingers pressed to his carotid artery. She looks up, her expression grim. "He is gone."

}
"Daren..." Kate says, steadying him with a hand on his pauldron. "The fight is not over. Stay focused."

"Understood," Daren says, his face hardening as he squares his shoulders toward the captain. "Cover my advance."

"On it," Kate says, launching a volley of icicles to test the captain's shield.

Flower and Illuna open fire with ranged spells while I loose bolts with my crossbow. Kate and Illuna are nearing the bottom of their mana pools, but Flower continues channeling full-power fire constructs.

#if(v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 0) {
Under our covering fire, Daren charges the captain. He extends his left hand; the broadsword rips from the gutter and snaps into his grip. The captain raises both hands, throwing kinetic shockwaves to keep Daren at bay.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_uninjured == 1) {
Under our covering fire, Daren charges the captain. He extends his left hand; the broadsword rips from the captain's belt and snaps into his grip. The captain raises both hands, throwing kinetic shockwaves to keep Daren at bay.

}
