"We do not retreat, coward!" the voice roars. "We avenge our captain!"

}
choice(""Then how about you actually avenge your captain instead of hiding like a wimp?"", B3-Ch06b-Tamper, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Tamper, v_b3_ch6_coward = 0)
choice(""Can't you just use your own teleportation device to cancel what Gontrok's doing?"", B3-Ch06b-Tamper, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Tamper, v_b3_ch6_coward = 1)
choice(""Yeah, Gontrok, don't be a coward! Stay here and fight like a man!"", B3-Ch06b-Tamper, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Tamper, v_b3_ch6_coward = 2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Tamper
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_coward == 0) {
"Then how about you actually avenge your captain instead of hiding like a wimp?" I call out.

"Hah!" Gontrok laughs mid-parry, fingers clicking through dial settings. "The kid has a point. You lurk in shadows the entire battle and preach courage? Step into the street and stop me!"

"Gontrok, final warning," the voice snarls. "Do not engage that beacon."

"Or what? Another phantom illusion?"

"No. I will--"

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_coward == 1) {
"Can't you just use your own teleportation device to cancel what Gontrok's doing?" I call out.

"He cannot override a thing," Gontrok barks, fingers clicking through dial settings. "Only the captain held master override, and he is lying in the gutter. I do as I please."

"Gontrok, final warning," the voice snarls. "Do not engage that beacon."

"Or what? Another phantom illusion?"

"No. I will--"

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_coward == 2) {
"Yeah, Gontrok, don't be a coward! Stay here and fight like a man!" I shout.

"Next time we meet, you are first on my list, smart-ass," Gontrok snaps, fingers clicking through dial settings. "We will see who cowers then!"

"Gontrok, final warning," the voice snarls. "Do not engage that beacon."

"Or what? Another phantom illusion?"

"No. I will--"

}
"Too late!" Gontrok slams his palm over the brass housing.

Blinding white light wraps around every surviving royal guard on the field.

"You will hang for this, traitor!" the voice roars from a second-story window where a matching beacon flares.

"We will see," Gontrok grunts.

Hadrik throws a furious overhand smash, but his fist passes through empty air as Gontrok's silhouette dissolves into light.

#if(v_b3_ch6_earth == 0) {
Five residual boulders hover overhead, drifting as their suspension fields decay.

"Watch the sky!" I call out. "Debris coming down!"

"I have them!" Flower ignites her fire jets, rocketing into the air.

She detonates the falling rocks with rapid fireball strikes, showering the street in harmless dust. Daren angles his shield to deflect the falling gravel as Flower touches down with a grin.

'Is it over?...' Leila writes, eyes scanning the quiet street. 'Are they gone?'

"The royal guards are gone, yes," Melindra says.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_earth == 1) {
'Is it over?...' Leila writes, eyes scanning the quiet street. 'Are they gone?'

"The royal guards are gone, yes," Melindra says.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Opportunity, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Opportunity) if (v_b3_ch6_plan == 3)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Mention, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Mention) if (v_b3_ch6_kelrim == 1 && v_b3_ch6_plan != 3)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Reveals, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Reveals) if (v_b3_ch6_kelrim != 1 && v_b3_ch6_plan != 3)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Opportunity
TEXT:

"Is everyone breathing?" Rose's anxious voice comes over the transceiver. "Please tell me no one died!"

"We are all alive, Rose," Kate says. "Your intervention saved the line. How did you gauge the timing?"

"I called earlier to say I could manage one more time freeze," Rose explains. "When I heard the clash, I held on the line, waiting for the critical moment so I wouldn't shatter your focus."

"Your call was flawless," Daren says. "We would be corpses without it."

"Your contact on the line..." Kelrim mutters, rubbing his forehead. "She froze time? That is how you unraveled the captain's technique?"

"You were caught in the stasis field as well," Daren says. "Rose bought us the window to-- Kelrim, you look pale. Or whatever passes for pale on green skin."

"I am fine..." Kelrim breathes. "Just... if she had not acted, I was about to trigger the neural overload spell. Seconds away from ending my life. The realization sits heavy."

#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 || v_b3_ch5_fight < 4) {
"Kelrim," Daren says gently, resting a heavy gauntlet on the goblin's shoulder. "Your resolve was noble, but the patients in the infirmary need you. They are waiting for your return. Do not forget that."

"Yes..." Kelrim manages a faint nod. "Thank you. Let us return to the base."

"Agreed," Daren says. "With the guards gone, signal interference should clear. Cluster close so Barry can lock coordinates."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0 && v_b3_ch5_fight >= 4) {
"Kelrim," Daren says gently, resting a heavy gauntlet on the goblin's shoulder. "Your resolve was noble, but the patients in the infirmary need you. They are waiting for your return. Do not forget that."

"Yes..." Kelrim manages a faint nod. "Thank you. Let us return to the base."

"About time," Albert says, stepping out of invisibility right beside our circle.

"Impeccable timing, Albert," I say. "Your support when we were being crushed into gravel was truly inspiring."

"Save your sarcasm," Albert says. "I took out the black-robed assassin. Did you expect me to solo the entire squad?"

"A distracting strike against the captain would have been appreciated," I counter.

"His aura sense would have spotted my approach twenty paces out," Albert says. "If I had a vector, I would have taken it. It was suicide."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 && v_b3_ch6_wounded == 1 || v_b3_ch6_wounded == 1 && v_b3_ch5_fight < 4) {
"Close this puncture before we jump," I tell Daren, nodding at my right shoulder as Hadrik lumbers over in dwarf form. "Bleeding stopped, but it throbs like hell."

"Right," Daren says, laying a palm over the wound. White healing light knits the muscle and skin. "Minor scrapes on the rest of us; I will tend to them in the infirmary."

With the wound sealed, Daren taps his transceiver to establish the relay.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 && v_b3_ch6_wounded == 0 || v_b3_ch6_wounded == 0 && v_b3_ch5_fight < 4) {
We form up on the cobblestones as Hadrik rejoins us in dwarf form. Daren pulls out his transceiver to establish the relay.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0 && v_b3_ch6_wounded == 1 && v_b3_ch5_fight >= 4) {
"Fine, fine, you played your hand," I say. "Thanks for the assist."

"Naturally," Albert says. "Tighten the circle so the operator can acquire our beacon."

"Close this puncture before we jump," I tell Daren, nodding at my right shoulder as Hadrik lumbers over in dwarf form. "Bleeding stopped, but it throbs like hell."

"Right," Daren says, laying a palm over the wound. White healing light knits the muscle and skin. "Minor scrapes on the rest of us; I will tend to them in the infirmary."

With the wound sealed, Daren taps his transceiver to establish the relay.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0 && v_b3_ch6_wounded == 0 && v_b3_ch5_fight >= 4) {
"Fine, fine, you played your hand," I say. "Thanks for the assist."

"Naturally," Albert says. "Tighten the circle so the operator can acquire our beacon."

We form up on the cobblestones as Hadrik rejoins us in dwarf form. Daren pulls out his transceiver to establish the relay.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Utterly, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Utterly)


