ID: B3-Ch06b-Fading
TEXT:

Daren reaches for his transceiver. Before his thumb touches the rune, a red-eyed drone drops like a stone from the clouds, slamming into the cobblestones three paces away. Its optical lens flickers out; the lift rotor sits dead.

"What in the world?..." Daren frowns, lowering the brass casing. "Malfunction? The rest are still hovering aloft, aren't they?"

"Aye, whole swarm is up there," Hadrik says, glancing skyward.

choice("Suggest getting closer to the drone, to investigate what happened.", B3-Ch06b-Curiosity, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Curiosity)
choice("Suggest running as far away from the drone as our legs can carry us.", B3-Ch06b-Carry, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Carry)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Curiosity
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch6_curiosity,1)
achievement("Curiosity killed the cat",v_ac_b3_ch6_curiosity)
"We might learn why the signal jammed if we inspect the chassis," I say.

"Wouldn't it be smarter to lock the teleport and go?" Daren asks.

"If the drone network is broadcasting the interference field, we need to know," I say. "Give me ten seconds."

I step toward the fallen sphere, circling the metal hull to check the power conduits.

Three rapid, high-pitched electronic chimes ring from the casing.

The internal core detonates. A blinding flash of thermite and shrapnel expands across the street, vaporizing our circle in a microsecond.

choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Carry
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim != 1 && v_b3_ch6_plan != 3) {
"Move!" I yell, breaking into an all-out sprint. "Put distance between us and that metal sphere now!"

"Why?" Daren shouts, falling into stride behind me. "What is it doing?"

"I don't know, and I am not staying to find out! Keep a rear shield active as we run!"

"You're the Overseer scholar!" Daren bellows. "Everyone, clear out! Rear defense is mine!"

We bolt down the avenue. Daren brings up the rear, projecting a broad aura barrier over our retreat. As he passes Kelrim's body, he scoops the goblin onto his right shoulder without breaking stride.

Behind us, three sharp chimes echo from the fallen sphere.

The drone's core detonates with apocalyptic force. A deafening shockwave tears through the avenue, blowing out second-story windows and gouging a scorched crater ten yards wide into the street.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim == 1 || v_b3_ch6_plan == 3) {
"Move!" I yell, breaking into an all-out sprint. "Put distance between us and that metal sphere now!"

"Why?" Daren shouts, falling into stride behind me. "What is it doing?"

"I don't know, and I am not staying to find out! Keep a rear shield active as we run!"

"You're the Overseer scholar!" Daren bellows. "Everyone, clear out! Rear defense is mine!"

We bolt down the avenue. Daren brings up the rear, projecting a broad aura barrier over our retreat.

Behind us, three sharp chimes echo from the fallen sphere.

The drone's core detonates with apocalyptic force. A deafening shockwave tears through the avenue, blowing out second-story windows and gouging a scorched crater ten yards wide into the street.

}
Even with our lead, the blast wave slams into Daren's barrier with bone-shaking force, but the reinforced aura absorbs the shrapnel. We skid to a halt, turning back to survey the smoking crater and the shattered storefronts. High above, the remaining drones drift in placid formation, entirely indifferent to the devastation.

"Glad we listened to you," Daren pants, watching smoke curl from the scorched masonry. "Another ten paces closer and we would have been shredded."

"It isn't over," I say, eyes locked on the sky. "The Overseer found a loophole around his maintenance lockdown. He cannot fly them into combat, but he can drop them as gravity bombs until he runs out of inventory. Illuna, quench that crater so we can cross back."

"On it," Illuna murmurs, channeling a torrent of water into the smoking crater.

Steam billows into the air as the flood boils against glowing stone, cooling the bedrock to safe temperatures. Illuna dismisses the excess water with a flick of her fingers.

"Path cleared," Illuna reports.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Carry2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Carry2)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Carry2
TEXT:

"Good," I say. "Regroup at the perimeter before-- watch the sky! Falling ordnance!"

Two more drones plummet from the cloud base, slamming into the cobblestones near our path. We sprint for our original coordinates as Kate throws up a slab of reinforced ice and Daren locks his aura shield behind it.

The drones detonate on shorter fuses. Heat scythes through Kate's ice wall, but Daren's inner barrier holds the shockwave. We scramble into the depression of our original extraction point.

I glance upward to confirm my read.

The Overseer has zero lateral steering during maintenance mode. All he can do is release vertical drops. His fuse calibration improved on the second attempt, but our extraction pocket has no drones directly overhead. As long as we hold position, his gravity bombs cannot touch us.

"Hold this pocket," I tell the group. "The sky directly above us is clear."

#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 || v_b3_ch5_fight < 4) {
"Didn't expect the Overseer to level his own city streets," Hadrik grunts, surveying the rubble. "What a mess."

"His civilian-protection routine was purged," I reply. "Collateral damage means nothing to him now."

"I will contact the operator before another salvo drops," Daren says, pulling out the transceiver.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0 && v_b3_ch5_fight >= 4) {
"Didn't expect the Overseer to level his own city streets," Hadrik grunts, surveying the rubble. "What a mess."

"His civilian-protection routine was purged," I reply. "Collateral damage means nothing to him now."

"Sprinting away from an unexploded device was surprisingly competent for someone with your record," Albert says, dropping his invisibility veil. "Perhaps your tournament survival isn't entirely accidental."

"I assume turning invisible and running was your immediate instinct?" I say.

"Naturally."

"I will contact the operator before another salvo drops," Daren says, pulling out the transceiver.

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch06b-Utterly, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Utterly)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Utterly
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1) {
"Barry, do you read?" Daren speaks into the transceiver.

"Loud and clear!" Barry Thundercloud's voice crackles back. "You were the ones unresponsive on the last relay!"

"We have signal clarity now," Daren says. "The interference cleared."

"I overheard chatter about a royal guard encirclement before the link broke," the operator says. "What happened to the patrol?"

"The survivors executed an emergency beacon recall," Daren says. "Gontrok ordered a retreat once we felled their captain."

"The guard captain is dead?!" the operator gasps, utter shock in his voice.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 0) {
"Barry, do you read?" Daren speaks into the transceiver.

"You're alive?..." the operator replies, startled. "What happened to the royal guard battalion that had you pinned?"

"The survivors executed an emergency beacon recall," Daren says. "Gontrok ordered a retreat once we felled their captain."

"The guard captain is dead?!" the operator gasps, utter shock in his voice.

}
"Confirmed," Daren says. "Initiate the extraction sequence."

"Right away," the operator replies. "Holding coordinate lock now."

"So we leave the ambassador behind?..." Melindra asks casually.

"The ambassador?" Daren blinks, processing the question. "He is still on the field?..."

"The guards' recall beacons are tuned for royal personnel only," Melindra says. "They abandoned him in the empty house down the alley where the captain stashed him."

"Aye!" Hadrik perks up. "Now that you point it out, I feel his aura hiding a block away!"

choice("Go and kill the ambassador.", B3-Ch06b-Kill, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Kill, v_b3_ch6_ambassador = 1)
choice("Leave the ambassador alone.", B3-Ch06b-Leave, v_current_scene = B3-Ch06b-Leave, v_b3_ch6_ambassador = 0)


ID: B3-Ch06b-Kill
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch4_billy == 9 && v_b3_ch6_betrayed != 3) {
"I will tie up that loose end," I say, checking my crossbow. "I know the house."

"Barry, no time!" Daren calls out.

"Sixty seconds. Hold the relay!"

I sprint down the side alley, scanning the rooftops for lingering drones. The airspace over the safehouse is clear—no vertical drop threats in this quadrant.

Following the faint pulse of his aura, I reach the doorway, kick the latch open, and step inside. The ambassador cowers in the far corner, gripping an ornate dagger in trembling hands, his face pale with hatred.

"Take another step and I gut you!" he shrieks, brandishing the blade. "I will carve your throat! Stay back!"

"Save the performance, Ambassador," I say calmly, slotting a fresh bolt into the groove and closing the distance. "Deep down, you knew how this ledger balanced."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_betrayed == 3 || v_b3_ch4_billy != 9) {
"I will tie up that loose end," I say, checking my crossbow. "I know the house."

"Barry, no time!" Daren calls out.

"Sixty seconds. Hold the relay!"

Following the faint pulse of his aura, I reach the doorway, kick the latch open, and step inside. The ambassador cowers in the far corner, gripping an ornate dagger in trembling hands, his face pale with hatred.

"Take another step and I gut you!" he shrieks, brandishing the blade. "I will carve your throat! Stay back!"

"Save the performance, Ambassador," I say calmly, slotting a fresh bolt into the groove and closing the distance. "Deep down, you knew how this ledger balanced."

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim != 1 && v_b3_ch6_plan != 3) {
"What are you doing?!" he screams, retreating into the drywall. "Stay away from me, you... you peasant!"

"No, Ambassador," I say, leveling the crossbow at the bridge of his nose. "You are the peasant."

The trigger snaps. The bolt punches clean through his forehead, dropping him instantly. I turn on my heel and jog back to the extraction pocket where Daren and the others wait.

"Good, you're back," Daren says. "Form on me. Extraction is ready."

"So..." Hadrik grins as I step into the circle. "The ambassador is history?"

"Handled."

"I'll miss the poor bastard," Hadrik chuckles. "Hated his guts, but hearing him screech bloody murder every time he saw us always brightened the day."

"He lives on in your memory," I say.

"Aye. His screeching definitely will."

"Initiating jump, Barry," Daren says, cradling Kelrim's body with his left arm while holding the transceiver in his right.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim == 1 || v_b3_ch6_plan == 3) {
"What are you doing?!" he screams, retreating into the drywall. "Stay away from me, you... you peasant!"

"No, Ambassador," I say, leveling the crossbow at the bridge of his nose. "You are the peasant."

The trigger snaps. The bolt punches clean through his forehead, dropping him instantly. I turn on my heel and jog back to the extraction pocket where Daren and the others wait.

"Good, you're back," Daren says. "Form on me. Extraction is ready."

"So..." Hadrik grins as I step into the circle. "The ambassador is history?"

"Handled."

"I'll miss the poor bastard," Hadrik chuckles. "Hated his guts, but hearing him screech bloody murder every time he saw us always brightened the day."

"He lives on in your memory," I say.

"Aye. His screeching definitely will."

"Initiating jump, Barry," Daren says into the transceiver.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 && v_b3_ch6_kelrim != 1 && v_b3_ch6_plan != 3 || v_b3_ch5_fight < 4 && v_b3_ch6_kelrim != 1 && v_b3_ch6_plan != 3) {
White light envelops our circle. The spatial resonance hums through our teeth, and the street dissolves, reforming into the cool stone chamber of the rebel teleporter room beside Barry Thundercloud and Albert.

"What happened to Kelrim?..." the operator asks, staring at the goblin in Daren's arms.

"He gave his life so we could secure the cure," Daren says quietly. "The entire quarantine ward is in his debt."

The operator lowers his gaze in silence.

"I will carry Kelrim to the infirmary," Albert says, stepping forward. "His comrades will want to pay their respects."

"Ensure he receives proper rites," Daren says, passing the body to Albert with lingering hesitation.

"It will be handled," Albert says. "I must also report the captain's demise to our king. He will receive the news with mixed emotions given their past. Until next time."

Albert turns invisible alongside the goblin's body, his footfalls fading down the corridor.

}
#if(v_b3_ch6_kelrim == 1 && v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 || v_b3_ch6_kelrim == 1 && v_b3_ch5_fight < 4 || v_b3_ch6_plan == 3 && v_b3_ch6_preparing == 1 || v_b3_ch6_plan == 3 && v_b3_ch5_fight < 4) {
White light envelops our circle. The spatial resonance hums through our teeth, and the street dissolves, reforming into the cool stone chamber of the rebel teleporter room beside Barry Thundercloud and Albert.

"The captain is truly dead?..." the operator asks, looking at our bloodied armor in disbelief.

"Confirmed, but it was close," Daren says. "Could have tipped either way."

"Incredible..." the operator breathes. "Our standard doctrine was to flee on contact. We never engaged him without our elite vanguard."

"I must report the captain's demise to our king," Albert says. "He will receive the news with mixed emotions given their history. Farewell."

Albert turns invisible, his footfalls fading down the corridor.

"We should return to the infirmary," Daren says. "Thank you for the extraction, Barry."

"Any time," the operator replies as we file into the tunnel leading back to the base.

}
